{
  "dom_id": "step-q108300",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$ Given that $X∼{χ}^{2}(4),$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X\\le x)=0.025.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $\\,0.072\\,$ | $\\,0.115\\,$ | $\\,0.216\\,$ | $\\,0.352\\,$ | $\\,0.584\\,$ |\n| $4$ | $\\,0.207\\,$ | $\\,0.297\\,$ | $\\,0.484\\,$ | $\\,0.711\\,$ | $\\,1.064\\,$ |\n| $5$ | $\\,0.412\\,$ | $\\,0.554\\,$ | $\\,0.831\\,$ | $\\,1.145\\,$ | $\\,1.610\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "The table shows probabilities in the form $P(X>x).$ So first, we express the desired probability in this form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>x) & =1-P(X\\le x) \\\\  & =1-0.025 \\\\  & =0.975\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{χ}^{2}(4),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=4.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $\\,0.207\\,$ | $\\,0.297\\,$ | $\\,0.484\\,$ | $\\,0.711\\,$ | $\\,1.064\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X>0.484)=0.975.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=0.484.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
